{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>From the El of your father, etc.</b> The meaning is that it was from the Elohim of his father that he attained what he attained, and he alluded that the matter was in the merit of his father. And he prayed that likewise He would always be his help, and that is his saying <b>and may He help you</b>. And his saying <b>and et Shaddai</b> means: also the name Shaddai, which is the name that supports the aspect of the soul of Joseph, as is known to those who understand the secrets of the Torah — this too was his help, to save him from the daughter of a foreign El, and to bless him through it." "<b>Further,</b> it intends by saying <b>and may He help you and may He bless you</b> in this manner: even though El helped him and Shaddai exalted him to escape from sin, nevertheless they hold it as a merit upon him, and they are his help and they bless him as though the matter came from him. And go now and see what I explained (Psalms 37:33) on the verse ״HaShem will not leave him in his hand, and will not condemn him when he is judged.״" "<b>And by way of</b> mystical allusion, the verse alludes along the lines of what they said, of blessed memory (Berakhot 10a): one who hangs [his merits] on the merits of others — they hang [merits] for him on his own merit. And that is his saying <b>from the El of your father</b> — you hung the kindness attained for you on the merit of your father; by this, <b>and may He help you</b>, meaning the help will be credited to you by your own merit." "<b>Further,</b> he alludes along the lines of what they said, of blessed memory (Bava Batra 58a): a miracle is performed only for one who is destined to stand in his righteousness. And that is his saying <b>from the El of your father</b> you had this thing; and from now on <b>and may He help you</b> lest you stumble in a matter of perversion, to establish his miracle in a trustworthy place."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:50:56.180081158Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}